{"operations":[{"content":"The quorum of the general assembly is one third of the members present, as established by the amendment adopted 2 May 2026. Where the amendment of 2 May 2026 and the bylaws differ, the amendment applies.\n\nThe general assembly has a quorum when one third of the members are present[[cite:obs-8c9f6126e0334f702f6fa58dad16e41a3674e4c6 \"Section Quorum is amended: the general assembly has a quorum when one third of the members are present.\"]].\n\nThe bylaws state that the general assembly has a quorum when one half of the members are present[[cite:obs-3a0a3e512ba9bb7b6e1ba68d2a91c4d315d72250 \"The general assembly has a quorum when one half of the members are present.\"]].","expected_sha256":"436a15c7e3320d188ca4600961246fbd84f9499c7fef4c72f7d8c338d24b363","kind":"modify","path":"doc/quorum.md"}],"rationale":"Added the quorum definition from the 2 May 2026 amendment, noting it overrides the bylaws where they differ, with exact citations for both sources."}